# Stackra file contract:
# Purpose: what git never tracks in the console: everything stackra gen writes into .stackra/ and
#          the root shims of the generated tool configs, and the build, test and release output.
#          The committed contract, stackra.manifest.json, sits at the member root, outside
#          .stackra/.
# Boundary: ignore rules only; the subset of the root .gitignore this member relies on, repeated so
#           the folder keeps its rules when copied out of the workspace.
# Runtime: node
# Governing contract: Stackra ADR 0294 decision 10 (generated output is never authored), ADR 0295
#                     decision 5 (generated tool configs and their root shims)

# everything gen writes: the runtime entries, the gen modules, the tool configs, the service worker,
# the manifests and the Electron files
.stackra/*
# the root shims of the generated Vite, Vitest and Playwright configs, for tools that read only the
# member root
/vite.config.ts
/vitest.config.ts
/playwright.config.ts
# template only: the generated samples are committed so they can be read beside their source; a
# real project drops this line once `stackra gen` runs in it (the same change in every member and
# the root)
!.stackra/**
# Vite renderer and Electron main bundles, and the desktop installers under dist/desktop-release/
dist/
# Playwright's traces, screenshots and videos of failed journeys
test-results/
# Playwright's HTML report
playwright-report/
